    LORE-072: unclassified bucket compiled-by-design in audit matrix
    
    `lore audit` derived runbook_compiled from check_count > 0 for every row,
    so the unclassified catch-all bucket row reported False — read by external
    consumers (the h3-board PM cadence) as a compile gap that does not exist,
    filing recurring phantom rows.
    
    Fix in lore/__main__.py _audit_rows(): the bucket row's runbook_compiled
    becomes True — compiled-by-design. The bucket's registry runbook object IS
    compiled (signature, recovery ladder, guardrails); only its executable-
    checks list is empty BY DESIGN (LORE-051 keeps the bucket in the output,
    LORE-066 hard-codes checks=[] and skips 0-check classes in the validate
    history). The bucket row keeps bucket: true, check_count 0, command_count
    0, last_validated 'no data' — executability health stays readable from the
    counts; a compile_note now carries the explanation on the bucket row only
    (curated rows carry neither compile_note nor bucket, mirroring the LORE-051
    marker convention).
    
    Pins moved with the contract (the old pins derived from the same flipped
    field):
    - tests/test_lore051_audit_bucket.py: the md bucket row now renders
      '| True |' (shared runbook_compiled field).
    - tests/test_cli_surface.py: bucket rows assert compiled True; curated rows
      still assert the exact check_count > 0 identity.
    - skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md: documented the LORE-072 bucket exception
      next to the 'means a runbook exists' definition.
    
    Count sync (LORE-029): scripts/test-count.txt 579 -> 584; stale 579
    literals + the test-file count updated in CONTRIBUTING.md, README.md,
    docs/INSTALL.md, skills/lore-usage/SKILL.md.
    
    Verification: full suite 584 passed; ruff check + format clean;
    scripts/check-test-count.sh PASS (canonical=584, live=584); the LORE-072
    ARM — every row in `lore audit --format json` reports runbook_compiled
    true — proven red-first (pre-fix: 13/14, table bucket row rendered False)
    and green after.
    
    Addresses LORE-072.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
